 "relevance_note": "The paper studies tissues of one individually described patient with Tangier disease (\"The patient, a 38-yr-old male, is the 18th reported case of Tangier disease\"); no ABCA1 or any other variant is mentioned.",
 "method_note": "Hand extraction, no table transcription by script. 1977 physical-chemistry study of spleen, liver and splenic artery from a single patient; the abstract and some passages are column-interleaved in the conversion, so spans were taken from contiguous Methods/Results/Discussion text. The paper names no gene or variant, so the variants table is empty (no variant is tied to the patient, so no 'not reported' variant row either). n_patients_reported = 1 counts the one patient with a Tangier disease diagnosis (no ABCA1 variant is stated). Publication year is not printed (only received/revised dates 1976/1977), so year is null. study_type 'other' (laboratory study of one patient's tissues). Serum cholesterol 42 mg/dl and triglyceride 297 mg/dl are given without interpretation, so hypertriglyceridemia, low LDL and low cholesterol were not recorded. 'The liver appeared normal' (gross appearance at operation) was recorded as excluded abnormal liver appearance; it does not name size, so the hepatomegaly checklist item stays not reported. Yellow fatty streaking seen through the small-bowel serosa was recorded as observed but does not specify mucosal deposits, so that checklist item stays not reported. Splenic artery lesion-free is narrower than non-coronary atherosclerotic arterial disease, so that checklist item stays not reported. Hypersplenism does not specify thrombocytopenia. Control spleens (n = 3) are not patients and get no rows. No contradictions found.",
